(## 5. Summary of the Invention) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The present invention relates to a system and method for adaptive access control of digital documents using) Tj
T* (contextual security assessment. The invention is intended to address limitations associated with conventional) Tj
T* (document access management systems that rely primarily on predefined permissions and static authentication) Tj
T* (decisions.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (In one embodiment, the system comprises a document access request processing module, a user identity and) Tj
T* (permission verification module, a contextual risk assessment module, an access control decision engine, and an) Tj
T* (audit logging module. The system evaluates an access request using relevant parameters, which may include user) Tj
T* (permissions, device information, authentication status, access history, and detected behavioral patterns. Based on) Tj
T* (the evaluated conditions, the system determines whether access should be granted, restricted, subjected to) Tj
T* (additional verification, or denied.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (In another embodiment, the system dynamically reassesses access conditions during a document access session) Tj
T* (or when significant security-related events occur. The access control decision engine may update applicable) Tj
T* (permissions or initiate additional security measures when the assessed risk changes. The resulting decisions and) Tj
T* (associated security events may be recorded to support traceability, monitoring, and subsequent review.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (In an alternative embodiment, the system may be implemented as a web-based application, an enterprise document) Tj
T* (management component, a cloud-based security service, or an application programming interface integrated with) Tj
T* (an existing document repository. The contextual risk assessment may employ rule-based evaluation, statistical) Tj
T* (analysis, or machine-learning techniques, depending on the implementation requirements.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The proposed system aims to provide a coordinated mechanism for contextual risk evaluation and access) Tj
T* (enforcement, thereby improving the responsiveness and consistency of digital document protection. The particular) Tj
T* (technical implementation, operational parameters, and combination of features are to be defined in the detailed) Tj
T* (description and claims of the invention.) Tj
ET
