(### 6. Detailed Description) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The present invention relates to a system and method for adaptive access control of digital documents using) Tj
T* (contextual security assessment. The system is configured to evaluate document access requests, determine) Tj
T* (applicable access permissions, assess security-related conditions, and execute access control decisions based on) Tj
T* (the evaluation.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (#### 6.1 System Architecture) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (In one embodiment, the system comprises a user interface \(100\), an access request processor \(110\), an identity) Tj
T* (and permission verification module \(120\), a contextual data collection module \(130\), a risk assessment engine) Tj
T* (\(140\), an access control decision engine \(150\), a document access enforcement module \(160\), a document) Tj
T* (repository \(170\), and an audit logging module \(180\). The modules communicate through suitable software interfaces) Tj
T* (and may be deployed on a single computing device, a distributed computing environment, or a cloud-based) Tj
T* (infrastructure.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The user interface \(100\) enables a user to select a document and submit an access request. The access request) Tj
T* (processor \(110\) receives the request and extracts relevant information, including a user identifier, document) Tj
T* (identifier, requested operation, and available session information.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The identity and permission verification module \(120\) verifies the identity or authenticated session of the requesting) Tj
T* (user and retrieves the applicable access permissions. The contextual data collection module \(130\) obtains relevant) Tj
T* (security information, which may include device attributes, authentication status, access history, request frequency,) Tj
T* (and other permitted contextual indicators.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (#### 6.2 Contextual Risk Assessment) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The risk assessment engine \(140\) evaluates the collected information to determine a risk level associated with the) Tj
T* (access request. In one implementation, the engine applies predefined security rules and assigns risk values to) Tj
T* (selected indicators. In an alternative implementation, statistical or machine-learning techniques may be used to) Tj
T* (identify patterns associated with suspicious access behavior.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The engine produces a risk assessment result that is provided to the access control decision engine \(150\). The risk) Tj
T* (assessment result may include a risk score, a risk category, and the factors contributing to the assessment.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (#### 6.3 Access Control Decision and Enforcement) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The access control decision engine \(150\) evaluates the risk assessment result together with the user's permissions) Tj
T* (and the requested document operation. Based on the applicable policy, the engine determines an appropriate) Tj
T* (action, such as granting access, restricting an operation, requesting additional authentication, or denying the) Tj
T* (request.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The document access enforcement module \(160\) implements the resulting decision. When access is authorized, the) Tj
T* (module permits the requested operation through the applicable document repository interface. When access is) Tj
T* (restricted or denied, the module prevents the unauthorized operation and may initiate an additional verification) Tj
T* (procedure.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The document repository \(170\) stores or provides access to digital documents. The repository may be implemented) Tj
T* (using a local database, a file server, an enterprise document management platform, or a cloud storage service.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (#### 6.4 Audit Logging and Reassessment) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The audit logging module \(180\) records relevant events, which may include the access request, verification result,) Tj
T* (risk assessment outcome, decision taken, and enforcement result. Access to audit records is controlled according) Tj
T* (to the applicable security policy.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (In a further embodiment, the system reassesses access conditions when a predefined event occurs, such as a) Tj
T* (change in device context, a new authentication result, or detection of a suspicious access pattern. The system may) Tj
T* (then initiate a revised access decision and apply updated restrictions where appropriate.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (#### 6.5 Alternative Embodiments) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The system may be implemented as a web application, a server-side service, a software module integrated with an) Tj
T* (existing document management platform, or a cloud-based application programming interface. The risk assessment) Tj
T* (engine may employ rule-based logic, statistical techniques, machine-learning models, or a combination thereof.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The specific modules, assessment criteria, decision policies, communication interfaces, and deployment) Tj
T* (arrangements may vary according to the intended application without departing from the defined scope of the) Tj
T* (invention, subject to the limitations of the claims.) Tj
ET
