( 10. Applications) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The proposed system for adaptive access control of digital documents may be applied in environments where) Tj
T* (electronic documents contain confidential, sensitive, proprietary, or restricted information. The system can be) Tj
T* (integrated into existing document management infrastructure to evaluate access requests and enforce security) Tj
T* (policies based on user permissions and relevant contextual information.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (**10.1 Enterprise Document Management:** The system may be used by organizations to manage access to) Tj
T* (internal reports, business records, contracts, technical documentation, and other confidential corporate documents.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (**10.2 Healthcare Information Systems:** The system may be adapted to protect electronic medical records,) Tj
T* (diagnostic reports, and administrative healthcare documents by enforcing role-based permissions and additional) Tj
T* (security checks where appropriate.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (**10.3 Educational and Research Institutions:** Universities, research laboratories, and academic institutions may) Tj
T* (use the system to control access to research papers, unpublished findings, intellectual property disclosures, student) Tj
T* (records, and institutional documents.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (**10.4 Financial and Banking Environments:** The system may be incorporated into document management) Tj
T* (workflows involving financial reports, audit records, customer documentation, and internal compliance materials,) Tj
T* (subject to applicable regulatory requirements.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (**10.5 Government and Public Administration:** Government departments and public institutions may use the) Tj
T* (system to manage access to administrative records and restricted digital documents in accordance with applicable) Tj
T* (information security policies.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (**10.6 Cloud-Based Collaboration Platforms:** The system may be integrated with cloud storage services,) Tj
T* (collaborative workspaces, and enterprise content management applications to support contextual access evaluation) Tj
T* (across distributed working environments.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (**10.7 Intellectual Property and Legal Services:** Patent professionals, legal firms, research organizations, and) Tj
T* (innovation teams may use the system to control access to patent drafts, invention disclosures, confidential technical) Tj
T* (documents, and supporting evidence.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The system may be deployed as a standalone application, a server-side software service, a cloud-hosted security) Tj
T* (component, or an application programming interface integrated with an existing document repository. The precise) Tj
T* (implementation may be adapted according to the security requirements, scale, and operational environment of the) Tj
T* (intended application.) Tj
ET
