(11. Industrial Applicability) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The invention relates to the technical field of cybersecurity and digital document access management and is) Tj
T* (capable of practical implementation in information technology systems used by commercial, industrial, educational,) Tj
T* (healthcare, financial, legal, and public-sector organizations.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The system can be implemented using conventional computing hardware, including one or more processors,) Tj
T* (memory devices, persistent storage, and network communication interfaces, executing software instructions that) Tj
T* (implement contextual risk assessment and access control functions. It may be manufactured or configured as a) Tj
T* (software product, deployed as a server-based application, incorporated into an enterprise document management) Tj
T* (platform, or provided as a cloud-based service.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (In industrial use, the system receives document access requests, evaluates relevant authentication and contextual) Tj
T* (information, determines an access decision according to configured policies, and enforces the resulting decision.) Tj
T* (The system may also maintain audit records to support security monitoring and operational review.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The implementation can be adapted to different document repositories, organizational access policies, and) Tj
T* (computing environments. Its use may assist organizations in managing access to confidential information, applying) Tj
T* (security controls consistently, and maintaining records of document access events.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Accordingly, the described system is capable of practical use in information technology and digital information) Tj
T* (security operations. The precise industrial applicability and technical advantages depend on the final implementation) Tj
T* (and the features supported by the invention.) Tj
T* () Tj
